{
  "format": "optibench-workstation",
  "version": 1,
  "meta": {
    "appVersion": "0.1.0-alpha",
    "author": "Optibench examples",
    "created": "2026-11-19T00:00:00.000Z",
    "description": "A CMOS 555 astable (RA = 10 k, RB = 68 k, C1 = 2.2 uF, ~4.5 Hz) clocks a 4-bit counter set to modulus 10. The BCD outputs Q0..Q3 drive a BCD-to-7-segment decoder, whose segment outputs a..g light a common-cathode display through 270 ohm current-limiting resistors (~10 mA per segment). The display counts 0, 1, 2 ... 9, 0 ... Digital parts run from an implied 5 V supply referenced to ground; the counter RST input is tied low.",
    "dimension": "2d",
    "modified": "2026-11-19T00:00:00.000Z",
    "title": "Decade Counter on a 7-Segment Display"
  },
